<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's BCN in venture with Alliance Cap.</title>
<headline>Brazil's BCN in venture with Alliance Cap.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian private bank BCN has formed a joint venture with U.S.-based Alliance Capital Management, spokesmen for the local bank said.</p>
<p>The venture, to be called BCN Alliance Capital Management, is aimed at managing foreign and domestic mutual funds and assets in Brazil and, in a second stage, in Argentina, they said in a statement.</p>
<p>Further details will be provided at a news conference at 1000 local time/1300 GMT on July 1, the statement said.</p>
<p>BCN is Brazil's sixth private bank and showed a net profit of 140 million reais in 1996.</p>
<p>Alliance Capital Management is the biggest independent institutional asset manager in the U.S., administering over $183 billion in assets, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
